{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503049-vampires-and-sexual-attraction","id":1503049,"title":"Vampires and Sexual Attraction?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-14T12:06:05-08:00","id":1503049,"title":"Vampires and Sexual Attraction?","content":"Which book talks about this in V20 outside of the core rulebook? I could have sworn I remember reading Vampires can have sex, but do not experience sexual attraction and to them sex is just a tool and they derive full pleasure only from feeding. The exception to this is Toreadors and some Malkavians. But what is the consensus of V20? I got a lot of people telling me I am wrong and that vampires in V20 do experience sexual attraction and enjoy sex as much as they do feeding. Even when I use the pages in V20 about it, they say that proves their point which is confusing me as it states the pleasure from sex pales in comparison to feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T12:42:22-08:00","id":1503055,"title":"","content":"I don't have a rule, but I have a quote from someone on this forum (but I can't remember who).<br /> <br /> They basically said if Vampires didn't or couldn't have sex, ultimate it would be <i>easier</i> to enforce the Masquerade, not harder. For better or worse, a lot of the source material that inspires Vampire has to do with Vampires having sex. <br /> <br /> Not that it helps with roleplaying...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T12:44:53-08:00","id":1503057,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:serif\">&quot;Vampires have sex.&quot; </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">True. It\u2019s a great way to feed,</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">but carnal pleasures don\u2019t mean as much to the Kin</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">-</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">dred. Feeding, which vampires call \u201cthe Kiss,\u201d is an</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">incredibly intoxicating and erotic experience for Cain</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">-</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">ites and their victims. <b><u>Sex is great</u>,</b> but nothing truly</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">replaces the ecstasy of feeding for a vampire.</span>\u200b<br /> <br /> &quot;As much&quot; isn't the same as &quot;doesn't matter any more.&quot; So yeah. V20 says they can have and enjoy sex, but the kiss is an experience that feels better than sexual pleasure, so it doesn't measure up. As far as I'm seeing it, sex hasn't changed for them in any way, they just have a better option. In comparison, sex isn't as good. Even in reality, for all that the reproductive drive is a big thing, sex isn't the be-all and end-all of the whole world, depending on the circumstances and the individual some people do have things they prefer to sexual pleasure.<br /> <br /> Attraction itself seems to depend on the writers. Typically the books say vampires are dead and sex is meh, and then you run into them being written like they do. Vampires have been written with specific orientations and being drawn to physically attractive people. DAV20 mentions a mortal sacrifice who was specifically chosen because he would be fun in bed. Whether they experience sexual attraction or simply seek it out because they remember they enjoy it as an activity is up to you, but they do enjoy it. I go for it usually being extremely low-libido or nonexistent unless the blush is active, in which case their sex drive/attraction functions as it did when they were mortal.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it feels like the writers are just like the fans, where group A says vampires are walking corpses who shouldn't be able to fuck while group B ignores them and continues to write the vampires fucking, and since canon itself doesn't always match up and we are ultimately in charge of our own stories the answer is &quot;do <i>you</i> want vampires to experience sexual attraction?&quot; and then your players shut up and go along with your decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 02-14-2023, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T13:17:34-08:00","id":1503060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503049-vampires-and-sexual-attraction?p=1503055#post1503055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have a rule, but I have a quote from someone on this forum (but I can't remember who).<br /> <br /> They basically said if Vampires didn't or couldn't have sex, ultimate it would be <i>easier</i> to enforce the Masquerade, not harder. For better or worse, a lot of the source material that inspires Vampire has to do with Vampires having sex.<br /> <br /> Not that it helps with roleplaying...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There certainly is no question if they are capable of having sex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T13:23:28-08:00","id":1503061,"title":"","content":"I don't think there is a hard canonical answer on that distinction. It is something every ST and gaming group will determine on their own. We know that most vampires feeding on someone, and their victims being fed upon, is incredibly ecstatic (ignoring the exceptions like the Grip of the Damned and such). But the actual issue of sex is more nebulous.<br /> <br /> This is what I hold in my own chronicles: Vampires are corpses. Corpses do not have the biological functions or impulses of living humans. Sex would mean nothing to vampires physically. However, mentally their mind - still composed of their memories, habits, and emotional connections - still retains its beliefs from when they were arrive. This gradually declines over time. So a neonate would still react towards people who would have aroused or interested them while alive, but an elder has lost much of that and increasingly views humans like humans view livestock. Eventually the reality of being a corpse that preys on the living eliminates much of the residue personality and reactions from the time when they were alive. This does not mean that even an ancient, monstrous vampire could not somehow be driven to actual sexual passion - it is just very unlikely and should have a story behind it.<br /> <br /> Of course, Humanity - and sometimes other Paths - also has a role in this. A vampire who retains high Humanity, even if old, will likely retain more of their mortal mind, while even a young vampire whose Humanity is low will see people only as vessels of blood.<br /> <br /> I believe as long as a vampire is at Humanity 7 or above, they appear human. Their face appears flushed, they even appear to breathe, and I would also hold that if they wanted certain parts of their anatomy to work then it could do so. So actual physical sex is possible. At Humanity 6 and below, that is not the case. Corpses don't get aroused, self-lubricate, etc. The other thing is that vampires can spend blood to appear more human/alive. So even low Humanity vampires could simulate sex if &quot;needed&quot;.<br /> <br /> But at the end of the day, both vampires and their human victims would vastly prefer the act of the vampire feeding than any kind of sex act. Why would you willingly choose something that is less pleasurable and requires harder work to accomplish (and for a vampire isn't &quot;natural&quot;)? Most things involving sex is more a habit for the new vampire than anything else, and it'll erode as the vampire becomes more used to being a vampire than thinking themselves as a human with special dietary needs.<br /> <br /> Different STs, different gaming groups, different chronicles will approach the matter differently, and that is fine. But the above is how I handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T14:41:28-08:00","id":1503065,"title":"","content":"My hard and fast rule is vampires can get horny from humanity and some path (cathari, sin etc) rating 6+. I also allow for have sex merit similar to eat food. I also tend to hard rule that anyone with appearance 6 can stir a vampires dead heart. Most sexual expression for them does come through feeding however.<br /> <br /> My current pc is pretty frisky as a Sabbat lasombra she mostly articulates it through mutual feeding. Being able to experiance the pleasure of being fed on and feeding on vampire blood while protected by vaulderie is quite a high from what the lore implies. To the point she's starting finding certain clans and types of human 'attractive' via vitae taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T21:19:13-08:00","id":1503106,"title":"","content":"V20 page 9, 269, and probably some others; Storyteller's Handbook page 20. That's all I could find after a 5 minute search.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T23:23:05-08:00","id":1503112,"title":"","content":"It's one of those maddening/weirdly personal things that touches on people's morals so it changes from author to author and storyteller to storyteller. On the human side of things most can't knock romance off the table if we want characters to be relatable, and romance for most people is affirmed by sex. sex is also common in vampire media as vampires are used to discuss taboo things<br /> and cassanova type vampires aren't supposed to be a weird minority and it doesn't make sense for them to have difficulties when they're doing it once a night. But on the otherhand you're a predatory magic walking corpse and your groin doesn't have any value beyond decoration and potentially excretion (there are at least a few references to beastial gangrel peeing to mark their territory. But you are also consuming a lot of blood which doesn't exit the body in most cases where it's used now that I think of it.) <br /> <br /> I personally can't imagine vampires not having sex, especially paths like Cathari/Sin on the table, and I feel like abusing your vampire powers to have wild orgies or unreasonably beautiful servants as a status symbol is something that at least an antagonist should be doing. That said, I understand why some wouldn't want your players doing that. Things like the blood bond also change from person to person. As some and I describe it, 3 points is better than real love, even if you sometimes get a little unhealthily obsessive, it'll bring you genuine joy and fulfilment which is quite absent in a lot of lives ; while others insist it's a false love and a gross violation of free will and thus expect only the worst from it.<br /> <br /> <b>Sex aside, I do think Vampires are going to be attracted to certain people</b>. As I run it, vampires gain attributes by feeding from people with superior qualities. Someone with a PHD from an elite school or an Olympian is going to be extremely &quot;nutritious&quot;, if a bit high profile to go after regularly. Idiot Savants and people with extreme physiological biases are the secret joys of vampire herds. but in general more attractive people correlate to having better physical and mental capabilities and are better for regular feedings (and also they make the vampire more attractive over time) This drives the disparity between vampires further, because the established vampires have great feeding advantages over the vampires feeding from the inept who fall through the cracks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T23:53:04-08:00","id":1503114,"title":"","content":"I basically agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> about vampires getting horny. I played in a chronicle once where the Setites had developed an herb which allowed vampires to feel sexual pleasure, but it was addictive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T10:22:48-08:00","id":1503148,"title":"","content":"I run it like Necroscope, where vampires are beasts first, walking corpses a distant second. Undead is not the same as dead. It's a distinct state as different from death as it is from life. So overly focusing on them being corpses doesn't really work, imo. Vampires are emotional creatures who have torrid affairs and ugly breakups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T13:21:57-08:00","id":1503160,"title":"","content":"I tend to think that previous sexual orientation influences feeding preference. Did you like men in your mortal life? Then your first instinct is to hunt after men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T16:13:57-08:00","id":1503181,"title":"","content":"Vampires do not experience the hormonal releases that characterize sexual attraction and gratification. Thus, their sexuality is only merely the memory of such. <br /> <br /> Can a male vampire get his thing up and go to work, acting out what he did in his mortal life? Yes. <br /> <br /> Will he ever again feel his pulse quicken in attraction? Feel the rush of endorphins as he consummates, and become lost in that one moment for eternity? No, never. It will become as pale and hollow to him as touching a fine fabric. <br /> <br /> Toreador who engage in sex probably do so for the above reason, Malkavians who do so are probably engaging in compulsion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T15:41:08-08:00","id":1503268,"title":"","content":"My rationale is that the Beast feels hunger towards humans, but the vampire's human side has no context for looking at other humans and feeling hunger, so they &quot;translate&quot; that into lust. Hence, vampires do get horny, after a fashion, and tend towards a form of bisexuality unless they try really hard to cling to their mortal preferences. I call it &quot;haemosexuality&quot;, even though people tend to groan and throw things at me when I do.<br /> <br /> V20 and DA20 states that they can have sex. V5 talks vaguely about them having to fake it below Humanity 8 (Frank Drebin: &quot;By the way, I faked my orgasms&quot;, anyone?). I suspect that they'll eventually abandon that once they realize how many players are ignoring it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T20:24:33-08:00","id":1503299,"title":"","content":"Our house-rule was that vampires were basically animated-corpses, that could have sex, if they wanted to, and spent a blood-point to be, &quot;Ready&quot;, but they don't have any sexual-attraction etc. <br /> <br /> Now, with the Beast, their might be, say found in those with a high-humanity, sexual-desires brought out by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T20:53:27-08:00","id":1503302,"title":"","content":"Personally I've never been all-in on the &quot;they are walking corpses&quot; thing. They are undead, not dead. Undeath is a distinct state, as different from death as it is from life. And vampires are passionate beasts in addition to being UNdead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T06:00:04-08:00","id":1503312,"title":"","content":"I think it definitely correlates to the kindreds humanity level as well. The lower the humanity the less they care about things other than predation/obsessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27749-welard","name":"Welard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T09:28:29-08:00","id":1503323,"title":"","content":"In the Revised Edition Player's Guide, there is an Essay on Love, Sex, and Romance in Vampire that I've always referenced when this comes up. It's a good read, several pages were published, if you have access to it. But unfortunately it was not included in the 20th Anniversary material.<br /> <br /> Essentially, it describes the kind of sexual attraction that Vampires feel as intellectual, rather than organic, or chemical. That what they experience is sensual pleasure, rather than sexual pleasure. They can physically perform the act, and it can even feel good, but it's not a physical imperative, instead it has been replaced with and pales in comparison to the ecstacy of the Kiss and the sharing of blood, so really, why would they desire to do anything else? They might use it in the hunt for blood, strategically, or it might be an echo of a desire rattling around in that mind, leftover from their mortal glory days. In the end, just do what feels right for you and your group!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27764-hasnamuss","user":"Hasnamuss","date":". 02-17-2023, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27764-hasnamuss","name":"Hasnamuss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27764_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T10:34:52-08:00","id":1503329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503049-vampires-and-sexual-attraction#post1503049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which book talks about this in V20 outside of the core rulebook? I could have sworn I remember reading Vampires can have sex, but do not experience sexual attraction and to them sex is just a tool and they derive full pleasure only from feeding. The exception to this is Toreadors and some Malkavians. But what is the consensus of V20? I got a lot of people telling me I am wrong and that vampires in V20 do experience sexual attraction and enjoy sex as much as they do feeding. Even when I use the pages in V20 about it, they say that proves their point which is confusing me as it states the pleasure from sex pales in comparison to feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I read the Kindred can definitely enjoy romantic and sensual moments with mortals, Ghouls (and Revenants as well, I would assume) and also between each other. But it is clear that for a Vampiress or a Vampire experiences and makes decisions and choices in regard to love, attraction, sensuality and romance with routines, schemes, outlooks emotions, and approaches that could be said to be - to describe it simply - extremely different compared to love and sensuality as practiced and experienced by mortals, or by Ghouls, or by Revenants.<br /> <br /> It might be needed for a Vampire to concentrate and use her Vitae or some other ability or skill in order to make her or his body and emotions function and work in desired and specific ways. As far as I have read, relatively normal sensual moments and situations are possible, but due to various reasons might be hard to achieve reliably or to full satisfaction. Some Vampires might find it particularly troublesome.<br /> <br /> Hence it is mentioned that the Kiss, the Blood Bond (including mutual Blood Bonding), complex and special arrangments with Ghouls or mortals, and also as well researching and developing more advanced techniques of rousing, drinking, and using Vitae are all a possibility.<br /> <br /> More intricate, rare, and advanced sensuality-related and love-themed skills and powers are also mentioned. Some of these might be specific to particular groups, faiths, and organizations - like Road of Sin, Path of the Cathari, and Path of Lilith, to give a few outright and commonly mentioned.<br /> <br /> The Discipline of Presence and some Blood Magic Rituals can also be used to help in regard to sensual and romantic notions and goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T10:36:53-08:00","id":1503387,"title":"","content":"My take is that while they could have sex if they want to, but it's more cold and calculating as they use there blood to mimic sexual arousal and the feeding is way more pleasurable and it get worse they get older and there ties to humanity get more strained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T09:04:17-08:00","id":1503757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1503049-vampires-and-sexual-attraction?p=1503387#post1503387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My take is that while they could have sex if they want to, but it's more cold and calculating as they use there blood to mimic sexual arousal and the feeding is way more pleasurable and it get worse they get older and there ties to humanity get more strained.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Vampires become older, more powerful, and also definitely more experienced, they probably manage to avoid outright problematic or difficult sensual or romantic situations through a combination of going through various interesting and special moments, experiences, conversations, discussions, and events.<br /> The Kindred can also depend on their immiediate social network - and also of course the groups, communities, and organizations they participate in - for emotional support, relationship advice and practical help in the matters of love, romance and friendship.<br /> <br /> All in all, I would say that the Kindred (and Ghouls, and also Revenants) can in the end, and through the passing nights and weeks and months, have nice, optimistic, positive, satisfying, and fulfilling romantic connections and relations of various categories and types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 03-03-2023, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}